        "Normal protein C levels",
        "Similar thrombotic risk but different anticoagulant protein affected"
      ]
    },
    {
      "diseaseId": "protein-s-deficiency",
      "distinguishingFeatures": [
        "Reduced protein S antigen or activity",
        "Normal protein C levels",
        "Similar clinical presentation but distinct protein deficiency"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "redFlags": [
    "Recurrent unprovoked venous thromboembolism at young age",
    "Neonatal purpura fulminans or severe skin necrosis",
    "Warfarin-induced skin necrosis shortly after anticoagulation initiation"
  ],
